      "message": "fix(sim): the span floor's tilt cap is closed at 90 degrees\n\n#1306's span floor read the interval bound for any span with an A/B\nletter at exactly +-90, because the cap that lets the samples bound the\nspan was strict. A blade-lying swarf link (B +90 -> -90) then pinned its\nhorizontal end's -R floor onto the B 45 pose's footprint, where the band\nstands about 34 mm over the tip: 18 false SweepHits in the release\nlane's full-band swarf tests.\n\nOn the closed cap cos A and cos B stay >= 0 along the lerp and\nln cos A + ln cos B is concave, so cos(tilt) is least at an end, by\ncontinuity also at an end where it is 0: the samples still bound the\nspan. Letters past 90 keep the interval floor.\n\nPinned by verify::sweep::tests::a_swing_through_vertical_reads_no_floor_from_its_horizontal_ends\nand the closed-cap brute lerp in tilt_span's cap test; both fail on the\nstrict cap.\n\nFixes #1404\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
